+ #### Output contract
+
+ Dispatch schema: [packages/mcp-server/src/schemas/artifact.certify.output.json](../../packages/mcp-server/src/schemas/artifact.certify.output.json).
+
+ Certification of a Forge NormalizedVizSpec. Cartesian charts use the existing Vega-Lite profile; ECharts-primary charts with matching data use the declared operand profile without a Vega compile leg. Both report coverage certified and a boolean folded conformance verdict. The operand profile requires passing a11y-equivalence, stable determinism, contrast neither fail nor ungradeable, and at least one evaluated clean accuracy rule. Spec-only ECharts calls remain uncertified with conformant null and explicit missing-operand notes. Findings, not-applicable rules, rule counts and per-pillar verdicts expose what actually ran; evaluator or render faults never become a passing operand verdict. Render determinism identifies the projected option and independently repeated normalized SVG where available, within the certified runtime matrix; a geometry-free bubble map retains only its option proof with its stated limitation.
+
+ | Parameter / field | Type | Required in this branch | Default | Description / constraints |
+ |---|---|---|---|---|
+ | `status` | `"ok"` or `"error"` | Yes | — | Whether certification ran. 'error' means the input was not a valid NormalizedVizSpec IR. |
+ | `coverage` | `"certified"` or `"uncertified"` | No | — | Certified identifies the Cartesian or declared ECharts data-operand profile, not a passing result: read conformant and the pillars. Uncertified identifies a spec-only ECharts call or an unmodeled mark. Spec-only ECharts contrast may still be reconstructed or exempt, while data-dependent a11y, determinism and accuracy remain unchecked. Absent on error. |
+ | `conformant` | boolean or null | No | — | Boolean for a certified profile; null for uncertified calls; absent on error. The ECharts operand profile is true only when a11y-equivalence passes, determinism is stable, contrast is neither fail nor ungradeable, and accuracy passes with rulesEvaluated greater than zero and no accuracy findings. Error-severity a11y findings and evaluation faults fail that pillar; ordinary warning findings and not-applicable rules do not. Cartesian behavior is unchanged: its four pillars fold together, with contrast/accuracy fail or ungradeable preventing conformance. Accuracy unchecked cannot pass the operand profile. A measured false is retained, never converted into uncertified. |
+ | `findings` | array of ref `"#/$defs/finding"` | No | — | One entry per failing a11y-equivalence or accuracy rule, at native severity. A11y codes use OODS-A11Y-<rule.id>; accuracy codes use their registered OODS-V codes. Warnings remain visible without failing a11y, while error-severity a11y findings and any accuracy findings prevent operand conformance. An evaluator fault is reported separately in the pillar and notes, so empty findings alone never imply a pass. |
+ | `a11yNotApplicable` | array of object | No | — | One entry per a11y-equivalence rule whose declared precondition was absent, in rule order with the precondition named. Present, possibly empty, when the ECharts operand engine returns the complete rule population; absent without data, on Cartesian calls, on tool error, or when the engine throws or returns an incomplete population. An individual rule evaluator fault retains the completed engine population and native findings, while failing the a11y pillar. Not-applicable rules never enter findings and are not counted as failures. |
+ | `accuracySummary` | object | No | — | How the accuracy pillar was reached. Present when rules completed: on Cartesian calls and ECharts calls with data. Absent without an ECharts operand or on an evaluator fault. rulesEvaluated counts resolved rule operands; a rule whose precondition is absent is not counted and explains why in notes. The ECharts operand profile requires at least one evaluated rule and zero failing rules.; additionalProperties: `false` |
+ | `determinism` | object | No | — | Re-emit and render determinism proof. Cartesian results identify the canonical Vega-Lite compile with contentHash and, when rendering occurred, the first normalized SVG with renderHash. ECharts-primary results are present when the `data` operand was supplied: contentHash identifies the retained projected option, and renderHash is present whenever that projected option was rendered successfully. In both families `stable` folds two independent emissions and, when renderHash is present, two independent normalized renders. A typed first-render fault keeps contentHash, omits renderHash, and makes stable false; bubble_map without inline geometry keeps the option proof and names the no-server-map limitation. Absent on the error path and on an ECharts verdict with no operand.; additionalProperties: `false` |
+ | `pillars` | object | No | — | Per-pillar verdicts on successful tool responses, including nonconformant results. Data-backed ECharts calls grade a11y over the shared operand-built table/narrative, repeat option emission and available rendering for determinism, measure or exempt contrast, and run the per-type accuracy rules. Spec-only ECharts calls keep data-dependent pillars unchecked and retain legacy contrast behavior. A fault cannot silently produce a passing profile.; additionalProperties: `false` |
+ | `contrastNote` | string | No | — | Contrast rationale naming the exact theme/brand. Cartesian and data-backed categorical ECharts results grade rendered paints against that CSS scope canvas; geo and continuous heatmap results remain exempt. Spec-only ECharts calls reconstruct scoped baked colors and make no rendered-carrier measurement claim. For exempt results, no canvas ratio is graded. |
+ | `notes` | array of string | No | — | Path-specific scope and missing-operand explanations, runtime-matrix limits, unmet rule preconditions and evaluator faults. The operand note describes the enforced profile; the spec-only note explains why coverage remains uncertified and conformant null. Empty offered/resolved rule sets remain explicit and cannot pass the operand profile. |
+ | `errors` | array of ref `"#/$defs/finding"` | No | — | Present and non-empty when status is 'error' (the input was not a valid NormalizedVizSpec IR). |
+ | `contrastResults` | array of object | No | — | The contrast row for this call's requested theme/brand. Collect rows from separate scope calls to compare themes. measured is true only for a successful render-backed categorical evaluation (pass or fail); exempt, unchecked, ungradeable and spec-only palette reconstruction do not claim a completed canvas ratio measurement.; minItems: `1`; maxItems: `1` |
+ | `accuracyRules` | array of `"OODS-V150"` or `"OODS-V151"` or `"OODS-V152"` or `"OODS-V153"` or `"OODS-V154"` or `"OODS-V155"` or `"OODS-V156"` or `"OODS-V157"` or `"OODS-V158"` or `"OODS-V159"` or `"OODS-V168"` or `"OODS-V169"` or `"OODS-V170"` or `"OODS-V171"` or `"OODS-V172"` or `"OODS-V173"` | No | — | Offered accuracy rule codes for this chart type. This closed set is distinct from accuracySummary.rulesEvaluated, which counts resolved operands; an empty array means no rule is offered.; uniqueItems: `true` |
+
+ Required keys in this branch: `"status"`.
+
+ Additional properties: `false`.
